Vendored rather than loaded from a CDN: a storefront should not make a
third-party request per checkout, and a vendored file cannot change under us.

The WithUtils build is taken deliberately. getNumber() (E.164 output) and
isValidNumber() both require the utils half, so the 51 KB core build alone
cannot do what this form needs. The cost is size, which is paid back by loading
the whole thing LAZILY -- only when a customer actually opens the address form,
never on page load.

Only the webp sprites are vendored: intlTelInput.min.css references
../img/flags.webp and ../img/flags@2x.webp and nothing else. The png sprites in
the package are unreferenced by this stylesheet.

